so here's a question I get quite a lot  how do I find my why well there are many  ways to find it I even wrote a book  called find your why to help people find  it but here's a really fun little  exercise that anyone can do called the  friends exercise don't do this with a  spouse don't do this with a family  member those relationships are too close  do it with a best friend and ask them  the simple question why are we friends  and they're going to start by describing  you I don't know they're gonna say  you're always there for me I can trust  you and you have to play Devil's  Advocate good you say that's just the  definition of a friend what specifically  is it about me  that I know you'd be there for me no  matter what and eventually they'll start  describing themselves and I got  goosebumps in fact I'm getting them  right now because what they're doing is  articulating the value you have in their  lives and you will have an emotional  response you'll either get goosebumps or  you'll well up and this is when you know  you're in the Wheelhouse you're in the  ballpark for what your why is
 

